# SEO-based site structure (Figsumo)

Always treat FigSumo as an SEO-first calculator site. Do not flatten tools into hash-only sections without a real URL. Brand spelling is **FigSumo**; canonical host is apex `https://figsumo.com` (www redirects to non-www).

## URL & IA

- One tool = one route: `/[tool]-calculator` (e.g. `/scientific-calculator`).
- Category hubs from the center navbar: `/financial-calculators`, `/fitness-health-calculators`, `/math-calculators`, `/other-calculators`, `/calculators-for-your-site`.
- Nav taxonomy lives in `lib/calculators.ts` — keep Header submenu, category pages, and sitemap in sync with it.
- Home `/` is the brand hub: featured tools, clear internal links, not a dump of every widget without copy.
- Keep utility pages: `/about`, `/privacy`, `/contact`.
- Prefer `next/link` for internal links. Footer and header must expose the main crawl paths.
- Calculator implementations live in `lib/calc/defs/*` + `lib/calc/registry.ts`; keep taxonomy slugs in sync.
- Prefer formula accuracy tests via `npm run test:calcs` when changing calc math.

## Per-page SEO

- Unique `title` + `description` via the App Router `metadata` API (use `lib/seo.ts` helpers).
- One clear `h1` per page. Use semantic landmarks: `header`, `main`, `footer`, `article`/`section`.
- Tool pages include: interactive calculator + short unique explanatory copy (what it does, how to use). No thin duplicate pages.
- Keep `app/sitemap.ts` and `app/robots.ts` in sync when adding routes.
- Add JSON-LD (`WebSite` on home, `WebApplication` / `SoftwareApplication` on tools) via shared helpers.

## Content rules

- Original copy only — do not scrape or mirror other calculator sites’ Q&A or sitemaps.
- Brand/text theme stays as configured (`#101010` text, `#2563EB` brand, light backgrounds); SEO structure does not override design tokens.
- Accuracy and lightness over “vibe” filler; useful headings beat keyword stuffing.
